      "worked": "The variable base requires $x>0$ and $x\\ne1$. Let $u=\\log_4x$, so $u\\ne0$. By change of base,\n\n$$\\log_x16=\\frac{\\log_4 16}{\\log_4 x}=\\frac2u.$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u-\\frac2u&=1\\\\u^2-u-2&=0\\\\(u-2)(u+1)&=0\\\\u&=2\\text{ or }-1\\\\x&=16\\text{ or }\\frac14\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values are positive and different from $1$, so both are valid.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
